§8: the `<table>` extras are the §9.1 decorator line above the table — the
layers inside it (caption, column, row, cell, foot) carry their own heads, so no
line *inside* a table configures the `<table>` itself:

@@tableX{.striped, sortable: true, #sales-2026, "Laporan Penjualan 2026"}
||@@captionX{.caption-note} Laporan Penjualan 2026||
| Produk     |      Harga |
| :--------- | ---------: |
| Laptop Pro | 15.000.000 |

A marker with no configured entry keeps the layer default; a table with no
decorator keeps working and its layers fall back to plain elements:

| Kolom A | Kolom B |
| ------- | ------- |
| satu    | dua     |
| ===     |         |
| total   | dua     |
